// clang_fpass_plugin.test — clang -fpass-plugin smoke (todo 36).
//
// Compiles a tiny device-only CUDA source through the real clang CUDA path
// with the pass plugin loaded via -fpass-plugin, and FileChecks the
// "kernscope.hello" marker in the emitted IR.
//
// CUDA root: the lit config stages a synthetic root (lit.cfg.py
// _stage_cuda_root — include/ from $CUDA_HOME + bin/ + nvvm/ from the nvcc
// package + the curand shim; the todo-5 fallback idiom, same as the verify
// ingester) because clang 21 only enables the CUDA language when it can
// detect an installation. -O1 runs the full default pipeline, so the EP
// callbacks (pipeline-start + peephole) fire exactly as they will for real
// GPU compiles with todos 37-41's passes.
//
// REQUIRES: no-gpu, cuda-root

; RUN: %clang -x cuda --cuda-device-only -nocudalib --no-cuda-version-check --cuda-path=%cuda_root --cuda-gpu-arch=sm_80 -O1 -fpass-plugin=%kernscope-pass-plugin -S -emit-llvm %S/Inputs/hello_kernel.cu -o - | FileCheck %s
; CHECK: define {{.*}} @hello_kernel
; CHECK: "kernscope.hello"
